*---------------------------------------------------------------
* entry.frame.equ -- syscall frame & copyin/copyout constants
* (task #3, docs/SYSCALL.md)
*---------------------------------------------------------------
FRAME_Y     equ   $0101
FRAME_X     equ   $0102
FRAME_A     equ   $0103
FRAME_P     equ   $0104
FRAME_PCL   equ   $0105
FRAME_PCH   equ   $0106
COPYIN_ENTRY  equ   $0100
COPYOUT_ENTRY equ   $0140
* K_LCBANK -- the interrupted process's LANGUAGE-CARD BANK, and
* the ONE cell here that deliberately lives in the PROCESS's
* zero
* page rather than main's. Every other cross-door cell was MOVED
* OUT of ZP because it was written with ALTZP=aux and read with
* ALTZP=main (docs/SYSCALL.md sec 7.5's second finding); this
* one
* is written aux and read aux ON PURPOSE. That is what makes it
* per-process storage for free: the doors write it into
* whichever
* bank was interrupted, and an exit path reads it back AFTER its
* own `sta ALTZPAUX`, which is by then the INCOMING process's
* zero page. No table, no pid index, no scheduler involvement.
* $00 = the default bank ($C08B), $80 = the other one ($C083) --
* the value RDLCBNK2 returns, stored unconverted. A fresh bank
* is
* zeroed, so a never-yet-run process reads as default,
* correctly.
* Reserved against user programs in inc/zp.equ; see
* docs/LANGUAGE-CARD.md for why the bank needs this and the
* write-enable cannot have it.
K_LCBANK    equ   $FF
K_RESULT    equ   $F3
K_RESULT_ERR equ  $F4
K_CPY_PROC  equ   $F7
K_CPY_MAIN  equ   $F9
K_CPY_LEN   equ   $FB
K_CPY_ERR   equ   $FC